      "reasoning": "Let's evaluate the starting hand.\n\
\n\
**Hand:** \n\
- Commune with Dinosaurs\n\
- Erratic Visionary\n\
- Island (x2)\n\
- Juggernaut\n\
- Savage Stomp\n\
- Scholar of the Lost Trove\n\
\n\
This is a 7-card hand with:\n\
\n\
- 2 lands (both Islands) — **problem**: I only have 1 Forest, but need green for Commune, Savage Stomp, and Scholar demands double blue.\n\
- Commune with Dinosaurs needs {G}, but I may not be able to cast it on turn 1.\n\
- Scholar of the Lost Trove costs {5}{U}{U} — extremely high; unlikely to cast early.\n\
- Juggernaut is a 5-drop artifact with aggressive attack requirement.\n\
- Savage Stomp is a solid fight spell, but costs {2}{G}.\n\
- Erratic Visionary is a 2-drop, but only one early play.\n\
\n\
**Problems:**\n\
- Only one Forest and two Islands — extremely poor mana base to support {G}, {U}{U}, {5}{U}{U}.\n\
- Almost no chance to play anything impactful on curve.\n\
- No early creature besides Erratic Visionary, and even that requires 2 mana with poor survivability.\n\
- Heavy in high-cost cards (3 cards of 5+ mana).\n\
\n\
**Decision:** This hand is too mana-screwed and top-heavy. I cannot cast any meaningful threat on curve and risk bricking for several turns.\n\
\n\
 => **Mulligan**\n\
\n\
