- Played Forest and Mountain\n\
- Cast Ironshell Beetle (2/2)\n\
- Has {1} mana up last turn, tapped both this turn\n\
- Beetle has summoning sickness\n\
- Likely a creature-based midrange or artifact deck\n\
\n\
### My choices:\n\
1. **Play a land** — I should, to keep up with curve.\n\
2. **Cast a spell** — options:\n\
   - **Aether Spellbomb** {1} — artifact, can bounce a creature or draw later\n\
   - **Erratic Visionary** {1}{U} — 1/3, draw-discard ability\n\
\n\
### Game plan:\n\
- I’m building toward **Thirst for Knowledge** on turn 4 — need 2 lands and a way to discard an artifact.\n\
- I already have **two artifacts** in play (Lightning-Core Excavator, and soon Aether Spellbomb).\n\
- Hedron Archive is a 4-drop I can play this turn if I lead with it.\n\
\n\
But **best use of turn 3**:\n\
- Play **Hedron Archive** — not listed as a choice yet, but I can play lands and cast spells in any order.\n\
\n\
Wait — **choices shown are only for casting**, not land play.\n\
\n\
The game says: \"Play spells and abilities\", but I still have a land drop.\n\
\n\
So I should **first play Hedron Archive** (as my land), then I’ll be able to cast something.\n\
\n\
But the interface presents land play and casting as separate decisions.\n\
\n\
Looking at choices:\n\
- Only two **spells** listed as castable: Aether Spellbomb and Erratic Visionary\n\
- But **Hedron Archive** is a land — I need to play it as my land drop.\n\
\n\
Ah — **Hedron Archive is a nonbasic land**, so I can play it as my land for the turn.\n\
\n\
And it’s **in hand**, but not listed in choices — why?\n\
\n\
Possibility: the game only shows **basic lands** automatically in land choices, but I still need to select nonbasics from the \"hand\" as a play action?\n\
\n\
But in MTG, you can play any land as your land drop.\n\
\n\
Let me check hand: Hedron Archive is in hand, {4} artifact, but also has land type? Wait — no.\n\
\n\
**Hedron Archive** is **not a land** — it’s an **artifact** with no land type.\n\
\n\
I **cannot** play it as a land.\n\
\n\
It costs {4}, so I cannot cast it yet.\n\
\n\
So I must play either **Forest** or nothing — but I already have a Forest and Island.\n\
\n\
I can play a **second Forest** to fix mana and power up future colorless costs.\n\
\n\
**Available lands in hand?** Not shown — but last turn I had Forest, now hand is: Aether Spellbomb, Ancestral Statue, Erratic Visionary, Hedron Archive, Meteor Golem, Thirst for Knowledge\n\
\n\
No **Forest** listed — I played it last turn.\n\
\n\
So: I have **no land in hand**.\n\
\n\
Therefore, I **cannot** play a land this turn — land drop is \"remaining: 1\", but I don’t have a land to play.\n\
\n\
So I must either:\n\
- Cast a spell, or\n\
- Pass\n\
\n\
### Castable spells:\n\
- **Aether Spellbomb** {1} — I can cast with {G} or {U}\n\
- **Erratic Visionary** {1}{U} — I can cast with {G}{U}\n\
\n\
### Decision:\n\
**Aether Spellbomb** is strictly better right now:\n\
- Costs less\n\
- Adds another artifact (helps Thirst)\n\
- Can bounce Ironshell Beetle if needed\n\
- Or be sacrificed later to draw\n\
\n\
