Or, I can sacrifice it for {1} to draw a card — but I need {1}, which I can pay with {G}, so:\n\
\n\
- Pay {G}: Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb, draw a card\n\
- Then I have {U} left\n\
\n\
But I lose the artifact, which is good for Thirst.\n\
\n\
But I get one card.\n\
\n\
**Cultivate** is better: gets me two lands, one into play.\n\
\n\
But if the system won't let me cast it, I can't.\n\
\n\
Given that it's not an option, I must work with what's available.\n\
\n\
Best of the listed options:\n\
- **Cast Erratic Visionary** {1}{U} — use {G}{U}, get a 1/3 flyer\n\
- It has tap-to-draw, but discard required\n\
\n\
Or:\n\
- Sacrifice Aether Spellbomb for {1} ({G}) to draw a card\n\
\n\
But sacrificing it means losing an artifact — and I have plenty, but it's still a tempo loss.\n\
\n\
Casting Erratic Visionary adds a body and future card draw.\n\
\n\
But still, **Cultivate is strictly superior**.\n\
\n\
Since I couldn't cast it earlier, and still can't, I suspect a UI issue.\n\
\n\
But to move forward, I'll **cast Erratic Visionary** as the best available.\n\
\n\
### Action: Cast Erratic Visionary\n\
\n\
