  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Mulliganing a 2-land hand that has a turn-2 Erratic Visionary (looter) to help find lands and colors. While the hand is color-starved (only Islands, no green or red), the Visionary provides card filtering starting turn 2, and in Limited, going to 6 is a significant cost.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to mulligan to 6 cards",
      "better_line": "Keep the 7-card hand. Erratic Visionary on turn 2 provides filtering to find green/red sources. If a Forest is found, Commune with Dinosaurs can find more lands. The hand is speculative but functional with its built-in card selection.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 2,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 2,
    },
    {
      "severity": "questionable",
      "description": "Keeping a 6-card hand with only one land (Forest) and almost all expensive cards (4+ mana). The hand has Thirst for Knowledge requiring blue mana that the single Forest can't produce, and the cheapest meaningful play is Lightning-Core Excavator (a 0/3). If they miss land drops for even one turn, this hand is unplayable.",
      "action_taken": "Kept a 1-land hand with expensive spells and color mismatches",
      "better_line": "Mulligan to 5 to find a more functional hand with at least 2 lands. A 1-land hand with this curve and no card selection that works with the available mana is likely to lose more games than a random 5-card hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 4,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 4,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed with exactly 1 untapped mana and Lightning-Core Excavator (cost {1}) as the only castable spell in postcombat main phase. There's no reason to hold the mana open - no instants cost {1} in hand, and the 0/3 body provides early blocking and artifact synergy with Thirst for Knowledge. Passing here wastes a free deployment opportunity.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in postcombat main phase, leaving 1 mana unused and Lightning-Core Excavator uncast.",
      "better_line": "Cast Lightning-Core Excavator for {1} to deploy a 0/3 blocker and artifact permanent at no cost, since the mana would otherwise go unused.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 16,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 7,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Player is stuck on 2 lands with a hand full of 4+ mana cards (Ancestral Statue, Hedron Archive, Meteor Golem). They declined to sacrifice Aether Spellbomb to draw a card, which could find a crucial land drop. The bounce mode requires {U} which they can't produce right now anyway (only Forest untapped), and the opponent's board (2/2 Ironshell Beetle) isn't a high-value bounce target.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, keeping Aether Spellbomb on the battlefield",
      "better_line": "Activate Aether Spellbomb's draw ability ({1}, sacrifice) using the untapped Forest to dig for a land. Being mana-screwed at 2 lands with a 4+ CMC hand makes finding lands the top priority.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 55,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 25,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Player passed with no other plays available instead of sacrificing Aether Spellbomb to draw a card for {1} (using the untapped Forest). With only 2 lands on board and a hand full of expensive cards (Hedron Archive at 4, Ancestral Statue at 4, Meteor Golem at 7), finding additional lands is critical. The Spellbomb's bounce mode requires {U} which isn't available this turn anyway, and the card draw to dig for lands is more valuable than holding a situational bounce effect while mana-starved.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn with an untapped Forest and unused Aether Spellbomb.",
      "better_line": "Activate Aether Spellbomb's '{1}, Sacrifice: Draw a card' ability using the untapped Forest to dig for lands while stuck on 2 lands with an expensive hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 59,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 27,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded a Forest while at only 3 lands on turn 7, keeping the expensive Double Vision (3RR) that requires 5 lands. Being mana-starved, keeping lands is critical to deploy the rest of the hand.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Forest to Thrill of Possibility",
      "better_line": "Discard Double Vision instead. At 3 lands on turn 7, reaching 5 mana for Double Vision is unlikely in a timely manner. Keeping both lands (Forest and Mountain) to play on consecutive turns would help cast Hungry Flames and a meaningful Wildwood Scourge much sooner.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 65,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 30,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed priority in precombat main phase with 2 untapped lands and Erratic Visionary castable for {1}{U}. The hand is very expensive (Meteor Golem 7, Hedron Archive 4, Ancestral Statue 4) and Erratic Visionary's looting ability would help filter towards lands and relevant cards. No reason to hold mana open with nothing to respond to.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Erratic Visionary for {1}{U} to develop the board and enable looting next turn to dig for lands needed for the expensive hand.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 80,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 38,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Passed priority in precombat main phase without casting Drover of the Mighty, a critical mana dork, when it was the only castable spell and the player desperately needs ramp to reach their expensive cards (Hedron Archive, Meteor Golem). The player is at 14 life falling behind with no board presence besides a 0/3 defender.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Drover of the Mighty for {1}{G} using Island and Forest. This provides a mana dork to accelerate toward Cultivate next turn (with 3+ mana) and eventually Hedron Archive and Meteor Golem.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 112,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 53,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Player passed priority in postcombat main phase with a castable Drover of the Mighty available and unused mana. Drover is a critical mana accelerant that would help cast the expensive cards in hand (Hedron Archive, Meteor Golem, Cultivate, Ancestral Statue). The player also still had a land drop remaining.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Drover of the Mighty for {1}{G} using Forest and Island. This deploys a mana dork that taps for any color, accelerating toward the powerful expensive cards in hand on subsequent turns.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 116,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 57,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attempted to activate Aether Spellbomb with an invalid mana plan, which was rolled back, resulting in no action taken. Meanwhile, Drover of the Mighty was castable for {1}{G} using Forest + Island and would have provided crucial mana ramp toward expensive threats like Meteor Golem and Hedron Archive. At 12 life vs 20 life, ramping is essential.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to activate Aether Spellbomb but failed due to invalid mana payment, resulting in no action.",
      "better_line": "Cast Drover of the Mighty for {1}{G} to establish a mana dork and begin ramping toward Hedron Archive and Meteor Golem.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 138,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 67,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Wildwood Scourge with X=0, meaning it enters as a 0/0 creature and immediately dies to state-based actions. The card is completely wasted for no benefit.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Wildwood Scourge with X=0, wasting the card as the Hydra dies immediately upon entering.",
      "better_line": "Hold Wildwood Scourge and pass. Wait for a future turn when more mana is available to cast it with X≥1 (or ideally X≥2+ for a meaningful body). The Scourge also synergizes with Nessian Hornbeetle and Ironshell Beetle's +1/+1 counters, making it even more valuable to cast later with enough counters to survive.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 154,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 73,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Qwen3L Rivals declined to block a 2/2 Ironshell Beetle with their 0/3 Lightning-Core Excavator. The Excavator would survive the block (takes 2 damage, has 3 toughness) and prevent 2 damage to the player who is at 12 life. With the opponent having Thermo-Alchemist and Chandra's Pyreling on board, preserving life total is important. There's no downside to this block.",
      "action_taken": "Did not block, taking 2 damage (going from 12 to 10 life).",
      "better_line": "Block the Ironshell Beetle with Lightning-Core Excavator. The Excavator survives and 2 damage is prevented for free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 161,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 77,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "The player attempted to cast Thirst for Knowledge with an invalid mana plan that included Ancestral Statue (a hand card, not a land) as a mana source, causing the game engine to roll back the cast. The player had 4 untapped lands (Forest, 2 Islands, Thriving Grove) and could easily have paid {2}{U} with correct tapping. The net result was wasting this priority window with no action taken.",
      "action_taken": "Attempted to cast Thirst for Knowledge with an illegal mana plan (tapping a card in hand), resulting in a rollback and no spell cast.",
      "better_line": "Cast Thirst for Knowledge using the correct mana plan — tap two Islands and the Forest (or Thriving Grove) to pay {2}{U}. This would draw 3 cards and help find answers while at 10 life facing growing threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 187,
      "player": "Qwen3L Rivals",
      "decision_index": 81,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Cast Double Vision with no instants or sorceries in hand to copy. The enchantment does nothing immediately and requires future spell draws to generate value. Meanwhile, opponent is at 10 life and QwCdr Proud is ahead - they should be pressing their advantage with creatures and attacks rather than investing 5 mana into a conditional future payoff.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Double Vision for {3}{R}{R}, using all available mana on a do-nothing enchantment with no spells in hand.",
      "better_line": "Cast Living Lightning ({3}{R}) + Nessian Hornbeetle ({1}{G}) for exactly 6 mana, deploying two creatures. Then activate Thermo-Alchemist for 1 damage (triggering Chandra's Pyreling), and attack with Pyreling and Ironshell Beetle for significant pressure against the 10-life opponent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 180,
      "player": "QwCdr Proud",
      "decision_index": 83,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Declined to activate Thermo-Alchemist with Double Vision on the stack. This wastes 1 free damage to the opponent (10→9 life) AND misses triggering Chandra's Pyreling's ability, which would give it +1/+0 and double strike for combat (turning it into a 2/3 double striker). With no instants or sorceries in hand, there's no way to untap the Alchemist later this turn, so this activation is purely free value.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Thermo-Alchemist",
